  "id": "monocular-deprivation",
  "term": "monocular deprivation",
  "definition": "Monocular deprivation is a research condition in which input through one eye is reduced during development. In the visual cortex, this causes weaker responses to the deprived eye and poorer spatial vision, and it is used to study how visual experience shapes brain circuits.",
